{
  "about": "Shared vectors for a window's picture settings per tile (docs/UX.md 'Digital zoom', 'Fill Tiles'): read by apps/macos NVRCoreTests (TileViewsTests.swift) and apps/windows NvrView.Tiles.Tests (TileViewsTests.cs) and NvrView.Shell.Tests. 'pan': TileZoom at 1x on a filled picture: 'zoom' and 'result' are [scale, center x, center y] (fractions of the picture), 'drag' is in tile units (the picture follows), 'zoomTo' zooms around the tile's middle instead, 'visible' is the part of the picture shown [x, y, width, height]. 'fill': operations on an empty window ('window' sets the window's Fill Tiles, 'tile' a tile's own choice, 'zoom' a tile's [scale, x, y]), then each tile's effective fill, the choices kept, whether the switch is mixed, and how many tiles are kept. 'tileIDs': the tile identities leaves have in reading order (null: none; a number: not a string) and the identities they get. 'saved': windows.json members of one window, and what is read back: the window's fill and the entries, oldest first, as [layout, tile, device, channel, lens, scale, x, y, fill or null]. 'migrate': a window saved in the old per-camera form ('tileViews'), the tiles of its layout in reading order as [tile, device, channel, lens] (device null: an empty tile), and the per-tile entries the views become, as in 'saved'.",
